<title>ISRAEL: Israeli forex reserves rose in December.</title>
<headline>Israeli forex reserves rose in December.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-01-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Israel's foreign currency reserves rose to $11.464 billion at the end of December, the Bank of Israel said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>			(in millions of dollars)</p>
<p>		  Dec 1996    Nov 1996    Dec 1995</p>
<p>Reserves	11,464	11,266	 8,158</p>
<p>The central bank attributed the increase to the government's raising money abroad during the month. Israel issued $200 million in Eurobonds in December.</p>
<p>- Tel Aviv newsroom, 9i72-3-537-2211</p>
